<title>USA: Itochu, Nissho Iwai to market Qatar LNG in Japan.</title>
<headline>Itochu, Nissho Iwai to market Qatar LNG in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFAX, Va. 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Corp said Tuesday Itochu Corp and Nissho Iwai Corp will actively market LNG in Japan from Qatar's Ras Laffan Liquefied Natural Gas Co Ltd and support project financing efforts.</p>
<p>In Tokyo, Itochu said the two companies had agreed to purchase interests in RasGas, which is currently 70 percent owned by state-owned Qatar General Petroleum Corp and 30 percent by Mobil. The firm is developing natural gas fields in the North Field offshore Qatar and expects to start supplying 2.4 million metric tonnes of LNG annually to the Korean Gas Corp in the summer of 1999.</p>
<p>Mobil said it and Qatar General Petroleum will reduce their interests to accommodate the Japanese trading companies.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
